.TH "xrdp-sesadmin" "8" "@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "xrdp team"
.SH NAME
xrdp\-sesadmin \- console XRDP sessions administration tool

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xrdp\-sesadmin
.RI [ options ]
.BI -c= command

.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page documents briefly the
.B xrdp\-sesadmin
command.
.PP
\fBxrdp\-sesadmin\fP is a console program to administer running XRDP sessions.

.SH OPTIONS
A summary of options is included below.
.TP
.BI \-u= username
Retained for compatibility, but ignored.

.TP
.BI \-p= password
Retained for compatibility, but ignored.

.TP
.BI \-i= port
The sesman \fIUNIX domain socket\fP to connect to.
Defaults to \fBsesman.socket\fP.
If no path is specified for the socket, a default of @socketdir@ is used.

.TP
.BI \-c= command
Specifies the \fIcommand\fP to execute on the server.
Valid commands are:
.RS 4
.TP
.B list
List active sessions for the current user.  Members of the
\fBTerminalServerAdmins\fR group can view active sessions for all users.
.TP
.BI kill: sid
Terminates the session with the given \fIsession id\fP, as shown by the
\fBlist\fP command. The session is sent a SIGTERM signal, and closes in
the same way as when the user logs out.
.IP
Users can terminate their own sessions. Members of the
\fBTerminalServerAdmins\fR group can terminate any session. If the session
does not exist, or belongs to another user, the command reports that there
is no such session.
.IP
Only processes which \fBxrdp\-sesman\fP knows to be sessions can be
terminated with this command.
.TP
.BR history [: \fIlines\fP]
Shows the last \fIlines\fP lines (default 20, at most 1000) of the
session audit log, oldest first. Only members of the
\fBTerminalServerAdmins\fR group can use this command, as the log shows
the logins of all users. The audit log is set with \fBAuditLog\fR in
\fBsesman.ini\fR(5).
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed. A message is written to standard error.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B xrdp\-sesadmin \-c=list
Show the sessions and their session ids.
.TP
.B xrdp\-sesadmin \-c=kill:3124
Terminate session 3124.
.TP
.B xrdp\-sesadmin \-c=history:50
Show the last 50 lines of the session audit log.

.SH FILES
xrdp\-sesadmin.log

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xrdp (8),
.BR sesman.ini (5).

More info on \fBxrdp\fR can be found on the
.UR @xrdphomeurl@
xrdp homepage
.UE
